  "dom_id": "step-q72856",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $K$ into the matrix $L$, where\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}K & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =L.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.\n$$",
